From f4329d72015fe0b6e4be666abc4f3c5a5fd2b5e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:10:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms: the vendor InfoFrame through the TMDS output of a
 dual-mode DP connector

A DisplayPort connector of a board can have a TMDS output of the GPU as well
as its DisplayPort one: the display table lists both for it. That is a
dual-mode port, and some laptops wire their HDMI port to one through a level
shifter (an HP ZBook 17 G6 with a Quadro RTX 4000: nvidia-drm calls it DP-2,
has two encoders on it, and the audio ELD that NVKMS builds says HDMI with
Supports_AI, which it writes only for a display that it drives as TMDS and
not through the DisplayPort library). Through that output the GPU sends HDMI
itself: NVKMS sends AVI, HDR and audio InfoFrames there as on an HDMI
connector.

The vendor InfoFrame of a client (HDMI VSIF metadata) was refused on any
connector whose type is not HDMI. Accept it also on the TMDS output of a
DisplayPort connector, while that output drives an HDMI sink: not through
the DisplayPort library, and the static display of the connector is HDMI
(nvDpyIsHdmiEvo()). The DisplayPort output of the same connector, a
DisplayPort display or an active converter behind it, still refuses it.

The decision is on plain values in nvkms-hades.h, so that a host test can
run every case.
---
 src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-hades.h | 57 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-hw-flip.c   | 31 ++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 87 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-hades.h

diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-hades.h b/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-hades.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..dc79c24
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-hades.h
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
